# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/)
# pages: the browser must check with the server on every visit (a quick "not modified" when nothing changed),
# so a new deploy shows up straight away and an old page is never served from the browser's cache
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# css and js: re-checked every visit here too, because their ?v= numbers in the sources are typed by hand.
# make-dist.sh switches these two to a one-year cache in dist/_headers, where stamp.py has put a content hash
# on every link (safe only when Cloudflare publishes dist/). "! Cache-Control" drops the rule above.
/css/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/js/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
